  "note": "Rokin 132-136, 134 and 130 (even side, on the water): a tall late-19th-c. red-brick front with cream speklagen and a two-storey white timber bay window, a dark brick 18th-c. cornice house over a shop (Rijksmonument: lijstgevel), and a black-painted bell gable over a white timber pui (bell gable in the register). The pand between 134 and 130 lies outside the buurt and has no strip."
